[38;2;124;124;124m3. None of $\overline{f_1}, \ldots, \overline{f_d} \in K[[X_1, \ldots, X_d]]$ is[0m[38;2;124;124;124mzero (where $\overline{f_i}$ is the image of $f_i$ under the map $S[[X]] \to [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mK[[X]]$ sending $S_j \mapsto 0$, i.e., the "constant term in $S$" or rather the [0m[38;2;124;124;124mimage modulo the maximal ideal of $S$).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mQuestion: Is $S[[X_1, \ldots, X_d]]/\mathfrak{P}$ necessarily finite over $S$?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this. This is related to the Weierstrass preparation theorem [0m[38;2;124;124;124mand its generalizations, and to questions about when a quotient of a power [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mseries ring is finite over a subring.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFirst, let me understand the setup. $S = K[[S_1, \ldots, S_n]]$ is a complete [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mlocal ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m} = (S_1, \ldots, S_n)$. The ring $R =[0m[38;2;124;124;124mS[[X_1, \ldots, X_d]]$ is also a complete local ring.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe condition $\overline{f_i} \neq 0$ means that $f_i \notin \mathfrak{m} R$, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mi.e., $f_i$ has a nonzero image in $R/\mathfrak{m}R = K[[X_1, \ldots, X_d]]$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mCondition 1: $\mathfrak{P} \cap S = 0$. This means $S$ embeds into $R/[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathfrak{P}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mCondition 2: $\operatorname{ht}(\mathfrak{P}) = d$. Since $R$ has dimension $n +[0m[38;2;124;124;124md$ (it's $K[[S_1, \ldots, S_n, X_1, \ldots, X_d]]$, dimension $n+d$), and $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathfrak{P}$ is generated by $d$ elements, by Krull's height theorem $[0m
